#
# File:         sdkconfig.defaults.mf35v2
# Module:       Build / ESP-IDF defaults, Makerfabs ESP32-S3 Parallel TFT 3.5" v2.0 layer
#
# Purpose:      What the Makerfabs ESP32-S3 Parallel TFT with Touch 3.5" v2.0
#               build changes from sdkconfig.defaults and
#               sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3. platformio.ini names this file for
#               the board's environments through SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS
#               (board_build.cmake_extra_args). IDF 5.3.1 still reads
#               "<file>.<target>" after each file it is given
#               (tools/cmake/kconfig.cmake), so the order is
#               sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, then this
#               file, and a later value wins.
#
#               The part (hardware v2.0): ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8, 8 MB OCTAL
#               PSRAM and the console on the chip's own USB, both exactly as
#               the S3 layer has them for the Waveshare stick, so this layer
#               sets nothing: it holds the board's notes, and is where a
#               setting of this board's own goes. (Its VFS line went into
#               the S3 layer's for every S3 at 1.2.1.) Sources are in src/board.h,
#               BBS_BOARD_MF_S3PAR35V2.
#
#               PlatformIO keeps the generated sdkconfig.<env>, a value it
#               already holds wins over this file, and it does not watch this
#               file: delete sdkconfig.makerfabs_s3_par35v2* after editing
#               here, and check the generated file. A value outside its
#               Kconfig range is discarded, not clamped.
#
# Targets:      ESP32-S3 (ESP-IDF 5.3.1)
# See also:     sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, platformio.ini
#
