# PSRAM: octal, 8 MB, as the S3 layer sets it. Nothing to change.

# The console: the chip's own USB (USB-Serial-JTAG), as the S3 layer sets
# it, NOT the v1.0's UART0. The bench board is cabled to the USB-NATIVE
# port, and with the console on UART0 that port is an output-only secondary,
# so Improv (and the web installer's Update) would not hear the browser
# there. The USB-TTL port (the CP2104 on UART0) still flashes through the
# ROM's own download mode; it shows the ROM's boot lines and nothing else.

# The VFS table is 12 on every S3 (sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, 1.2.1).
